+/// touching a real one. The text rides STDIN, never argv: process
+/// listings leak arguments, and the payload is a credential.
+///
+/// - macOS: `pbcopy`
+/// - Linux: `xclip -selection clipboard`, falling back to `wl-copy`
+///   (Wayland)
+/// - Windows: `clip`
